{
  "name": "Google Maps navigation - next-state cases",
  "provenance": "Case inputs follow the command template 'navigate from ${src} to ${dst} by ...' (mode = car, walk, public transportation). The captured source and destination addresses are templated as ${src} / ${dst}, matching map_tree.json; substitute real addresses to replay a concrete route. 'calls' is the UI operation history; its last element is the current state id from map_tree.json. 'options' is the set of next states the agent is choosing between at that step, taken from the map_tree.json transitions of the current state (s9 cases consider only the mode tabs plus the synthetic 'finish'). 'expected' is the outcome the loaded rules must produce: a next state, or 'ask_model' when the engine must fall back to the model. These cases are illustrative, NOT held-out evaluation data.",
